{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1560147-spider-fu","id":1560147,"title":"Spider-fu","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-05-21T22:23:58-07:00","id":1560147,"title":"Spider-fu","content":"I wanted to formalize some real-world spider tactics into combat maneuvers - mainly for the fun of it \u2013 but also because things like tackling and wrapping an opponent happened often enough for a house rule. So far my group resolved other combat situations specific to spider anatomy and abilities mostly narratively, aside from basic maneuvers such as Grapple, Bite, Claw and so on.<br /> <br /> However, Lilian and Pithus forms have a radically different physiology, and silk, venom, and extra limbs add to the options that few players would not want to utilize.<br /> <br /> Many of the specialized abilities of certain spider genera are available as Gifts (Web Sheet, Tarantula\u2019s Kiss, Waterwalk, Trap Door, etc) but there are also basic actions a spider can apply that I feel are missing.<br /> <br /> Spiders are grapplers. All spiders aim to immobilize their prey to consume it, with either webs, bites, or both. Ananasi can kick and punch as well, but there are plenty maneuvers for that already. I tried to make maneuvers \u2018click together\u2019 to create more of a fighting style rather than a loose collection.<br /> <br /> The Shapechanging Maneuvers are more of an exploration on how the Crawlerling form could be used in a Kailindo-like way with rapid changes. The form is unique enough that it warrants a look outside of size-changing maneuvers, but the results may be a bit too T-1000 coded.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Basic and Web Maneuvers</b><br /> <br /> <b>Spider Hug</b><b>:</b> The most basic spider maneuver. The Ananasi propels herself forward with hydraulic pressure to her legs, then extends all limbs like a grasping hand and tries to grip around the opponent to immobilize them.<br /> This works much like the Tackle maneuver, but if successful puts the opponent into a grappled state. The maneuver may also be performed from relatively close since the Ananasi does not need to build up momentum, or it can be initiated as a drop from a higher position.<br /> <b>Usable By:</b> Lilian, Pithus<br /> <b>Roll:</b> Dexterity + Athletics<br /> <b>Difficulty:</b> 7<br /> <b>Cost:</b> none<br /> <b>Damage:</b> Strength B (impact)<br /> <b>Actions:</b> 1<br /> <br /> <b>Envelop: </b>Must be performed on a grappled opponent. The Ananasi tries to maintain her grapple with six limbs, while her legs wrap the opponent into a neat package. The latter can still try to escape at this point, but may already have to struggle against the binding if their Initiative is lower. Ananasi web has Strength 9 and 3 health levels. Fully enveloped opponents may suffer from asphyxiation by the next turn, and restricted movement means pure strength may be the only option of escape.<br /> <b>Usable By:</b> Lilian, Pithus<br /> <b>Roll:</b> Stamina + Brawl + 1 (to maintain the Grapple)<br /> <b>Difficulty:</b> 6 (to maintain the Grapple)<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Blood Point for silk<br /> <b>Damage:</b> none<br /> <b>Actions:</b> 1<br /> <br /> <b>Grapple Bite:</b> Spiders deliberately target their fangs at soft spots, like joints, the \u2018neck\u2019, and any other gaps a prey\u2019s armor might offer. This becomes easier as part of a grappling maneuver \u2013 especially if the Ananasi has the back of her opponent. She may perform a Bite as part of the grapple action if she has at least two extra successes on the initial Grapple roll.<br /> <b>Usable By:</b> Lilian, Pithus<br /> <b>Roll:</b> Dexterity + Brawl<br /> <b>Difficulty:</b> 5<br /> <b>Cost:</b> none<br /> <b>Damage:</b> Strength + 1 A, venom damage<br /> <b>Actions:</b> none<br /> <br /> <b>Claw Down: </b>Must be performed on a grappled opponent. The Ananasi tries to maintain her grapple with six limbs, while using her front limbs to pound down on the opponent.<br /> <b>Usable By:</b> Lilian, Pithus<br /> <b>Roll:</b> Stamina + Brawl + 1 (to maintain the Grapple)<br /> <b>Difficulty:</b> 6 (to maintain the Grapple)<br /> <b>Cost:</b> none<br /> <b>Damage:</b> Strength + 2 A<br /> <b>Actions:</b> 1<br /> <br /> <b>Trip</b><b>w</b><b>ires: </b>While dodging attacks, the Ananasi simultaneously puts web strands into the environment that act as impromptu traps, making it more difficult for attackers to maneuver. She may also try to maneuver herself around an opponent to deliberately trip or entangle them. Subsequent successful dodges increase the difficulty of melee attacks on her by 1 each, to a maximum of 9 if the combat continues in the same area. A failed melee attack against her will result in a knockdown. Unfortunately, these demerits may also apply to unwary allies fighting alongside her.<br /> <b>Usable By:</b> Lilian, Pithus, Homid with Spinnerets<br /> <b>Roll:</b> as usual Dodge roll<br /> <b>Difficulty:</b> as usual Dodge roll<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Blood Point per scene<br /> <b>Damage:</b> none<br /> <b>Actions:</b> 1<br /> <br /> <b>Web Weapon:</b> The Ananasi can employ small measures of her web as simple weapons. While these usually do not do much direct damage, the surprise may be enough to literally trip an opponent up. Such improvised weapons may be a small tangle net, a garotte, or a strand of adhesive web slung like a whip or bola.<br /> <b>Usable By:</b> Lilian, Pithus, Homid with Spinnerets<br /> <b>Roll:</b> Dexterity + Melee<br /> <b>Difficulty:</b> 7<br /> <b>Cost:</b> none<br /> <b>Damage:</b> special<br /> <b>Actions:</b> 1<br /> <br /> <b>Riposte:</b> If the Ananasi\u2019s current form has more limbs than an attacker and her Initiative is higher, she may delay her action to deflect a melee attack and counter with -2 decreased difficulty.<br /> To be able to deflect an attack, it must not employ a weapon that out-ranges her leg (or arm/weapon) length.<br /> <b>Usable By:</b> Lilian, Pithus<br /> <b>Roll:</b> Dexterity + Brawl (or Melee) to deflect<br /> <b>Difficulty:</b> 7 to deflect, -2 on action<br /> <b>Cost:</b> none<br /> <b>Damage: </b>as chosen counter attack action<br /> <b>Actions:</b> 1<br /> <br /> <b>Kick </b><b>Off</b><b>:</b> The Anasasi may use her hydraulics to quickly disengage or escape a grapple by pushing all her limbs against an opponent. The main goal is to break off an attack and gain distance, but the disengagement might knock down or hurt the opponent.<br /> This is basically like a single-action use of the Hydraulic Strength Gift, but much more of an escape option than an attack.<br /> <b>Usable By:</b> Lilian, Pithus<br /> <b>Roll:</b> Dexterity + Brawl + 2<br /> <b>Difficulty:</b> 6 to disengage, contested roll to escape<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Blood Point<br /> <b>Damage: </b>Strength + 2 B<br /> <b>Actions:</b> 1<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Shapeshifting Maneuvers</b><br /> <br /> All shapeshifting maneuvers assume a quick change into Crawlerling form and back to the previous form. Since the reflexive change requires a Blood Point, these can not be performed if the Ananasi has already spent blood this round, unless she uses the Blood Pump Gift.<br /> <br /> <b>Crawlerling </b><b>Dodge:</b> If the Ananasi has a higher Initiative than her opponent, she may anticipate an incoming melee strike and dodge the damage completely by delaying her action and briefly dispersing into Crawlerlings.<br /> This maneuver can also be used when receiving a hit at lower Initiative to lessen the impact, downgrading the damage type by one category (to a minimum of Bashing damage). This uses the turn action of the Ananasi.<br /> The Ananasi may combo into one of the other shapeshifting maneuvers from Crawlerling form without the additional Blood Point cost if the roll had at least two extra successes.<br /> <b>Usable By:</b> Lilian, Pithus, Homid<br /> <b>Roll:</b> Dexterity + Athletics<br /> <b>Difficulty:</b> as usual Dodge roll<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Blood Point<br /> <b>Damage: </b>none<br /> <b>Actions:</b> 1<br /> <br /> <b>Reverse Hold: </b>Unless her opponent has found a way to hold onto a swarm of spiders, the Ananasi can automatically escape a grapple or other restraint, trying to reverse the situation by changing back in a position to grapple the opponent herself.<br /> While escape is automatic, a successful roll is necessary for a reversal.<br /> <b>Usable By:</b> Lilian, Pithus, Homid<br /> <b>Roll:</b> Dexterity + Brawl<br /> <b>Difficulty:</b> 7<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Blood Point<br /> <b>Damage: </b>none<br /> <b>Actions:</b> 1<br /> <br /> <b>Engulf: </b>as per CB20<br /> <br /> <b>Blink:</b> The Ananasi uses her momentary Crawlerling form to briefly crawl sideways and reposition herself for a flank attack or backstab.<br /> <b>Usable By:</b> Lilian, Pithus, Homid<br /> <b>Roll:</b> Gnosis<br /> <b>Difficulty:</b> Gauntlet (Web) + 1<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Blood Point<br /> <b>Damage: </b>none<br /> <b>Actions:</b> 1<br /> <br /> <b>Vex: </b>Similar to Engulf, but aims for sabotage instead of brute force. The Ananasi delivers a blow or kick that deposits a bunch of Crawlerlings on the opponent with a partial transformation, which then attack weak spots like eyes, fingers, mouth, ears and so on. The damage is negligible, but the bites still hurt and a dozen spiders in your clothes (or body orifices) is still distracting.<br /> The Ananasi can use this to Disarm or Blind, or simply create an opening.<br /> <b>Usable By:</b> Lilian, Pithus, Homid<br /> <b>Roll:</b> Dexterity + Brawl<br /> <b>Difficulty:</b> 7<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Blood Point<br /> <b>Damage: </b>Strength B (initial hit), special<br /> <b>Actions:</b> 1<br /> <br /> <br /> If you spot any bugs I built in, or think I missed something, let me know.<br /> <br /> Edit: Adjusted some Attributes and Difficulties as per discussion","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 05-26-2026, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-22T19:26:20-07:00","id":1560158,"title":"","content":"Technically the Crawlerling capabilities could be used by Camazotz where you're using them, since Microchiroptera form also allows them to change into a swarm.<br /> <br /> More concerning, though, is how any maneuver can beat the basic clinch, since Ananasi have claws and can therefore deal agg with their massive Might of Ananasa strength.<br /> <br /> As a word use note,<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, Lilian and Pithus forms have a radically different <b>physiognomy</b> </div> </div> </div>Physiology. Physiognomy is, at best, a reference to outward appearance, and more typically, is associated with phrenology or other pseudoscience efforts involving looking at surface features..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-23T02:09:22-07:00","id":1560160,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1560147-spider-fu?p=1560158#post1560158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Physiology. Physiognomy is, at best, a reference to outward appearance, and more typically, is associated with phrenology or other pseudoscience efforts involving looking at surface features..</div> </div> </div> </div>Corrected, thank you. Bad mistake to make.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1560147-spider-fu?p=1560158#post1560158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically the Crawlerling capabilities could be used by Camazotz where you're using them, since Microchiroptera form also allows them to change into a swarm.<br /> <br /> More concerning, though, is how any maneuver can beat the basic clinch, since Ananasi have claws and can therefore deal agg with their massive Might of Ananasa strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I thought about how to limit escape use. The mandatory Blood Point does that somewhat, and maybe an additional Gnosis point cost for situations where shapeshifting maneuvers are initiated when held - ie, the werespider has too little wiggle room to effectively change form and needs to employ 'extra space' from the penumbra*. Alternatively a +2 difficulty capped at 9 could work. I'm not sure which one would be more balanced.<br /> <br /> *Edit: I don't like this solution, because it implies form change could be prevented by restricting the changer. The problem is that swarm forms should be able to be used to escape with a normal change, so I need a good reason why it shouldn't work for an impromptu change. I'm drawing a blank on that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Question for everyone: I'm curious, have you made any homebrew maneuvers for Fera that use the particularities of their non-Homid forms?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 05-23-2026, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-24T14:32:17-07:00","id":1560182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1560147-spider-fu?p=1560160#post1560160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I thought about how to limit escape use. The mandatory Blood Point does that somewhat, and maybe an additional Gnosis point cost for situations where shapeshifting maneuvers are initiated when held - ie, the werespider has too little wiggle room to effectively change form and needs to employ 'extra space' from the penumbra*. Alternatively a +2 difficulty capped at 9 could work. I'm not sure which one would be more balanced.<br /> <br /> *Edit: I don't like this solution, because it implies form change could be prevented by restricting the changer. The problem is that swarm forms should be able to be used to escape with a normal change, so I need a good reason why it shouldn't work for an impromptu change. I'm drawing a blank on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was referring more to how it's incredibly easy to outright kill someone using a clinch, since you can double dip on any Strength enhancements you have (to hit and to damage) and claws turn the damage you do from bashing to agg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-24T16:16:24-07:00","id":1560186,"title":"","content":"Oh, I see. The pounce-tackle-hug maneuver I made already uses Dex and does Bashing, but I would have to houserule the standard Grapple/Clinch to use Dexterity, too. Makes more sense anyways.<br /> For maintaining a hold, Strength felt like the intuitive choice though. Maybe Stamina?<br /> <br /> To be honest, next to a Garou I never experienced Ananasi as dreadful combat machines. With prep time it's a different story, but surprise fights usually didn't go in their favor. IMO they need a bit of an edge they can fall back on in those situations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-26T01:33:28-07:00","id":1560224,"title":"","content":"Adjusted Attributes for hold rolls and upped the difficulty of some shapeshifitng maneuvers, looks better now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}